## Context

A multi-role web application built to streamline equipment lending and return administration for organizations such as laboratories, offices, or campus student associations.

## Problem

When equipment borrowing is tracked on paper or in chat groups, coordinators struggle to verify real-time item availability, prevent double borrowing, and maintain an accurate history of who borrowed each item and in what condition it was returned.

## My role

Owner: I mapped the borrowing and approval workflow across organizational roles, designed the MySQL schema (`pinjam.sql`), built the PHP web application, and deployed the containerized demo.

## As-is analysis

Equipment requests involve three distinct parties: borrowers who request items, division/operator staff who verify requests and returns, and administrators or treasurers who oversee inventory and reports. Handling these handoffs manually created bottlenecks and missing records.

## Requirements

- Multi-role access for Treasurer/Admin (`bendahara_dashboard.php`), Division/Operator (`divisi_dashboard.php`), and Borrower (`peminjam_dashboard.php`).
- Cart-based equipment request workflow (`add_to_chart.php`, `shopping-cart.php`, `checkout.php`) so borrowers can request multiple items in one submission.
- Approval verification, return tracking with item condition records, and per-user borrowing history.
- Centralized inventory management and borrowing activity reports.

## Solution design

The system adapts a familiar cart-and-checkout interaction model to organizational equipment lending, pairing it with role-based approval dashboards and a shared MySQL inventory ledger so availability updates cleanly as requests move through approval and return.

## Build

Built with PHP, MySQL, HTML/CSS/JavaScript, and Docker (`render.yaml` deployment at `peminjaman-alat-demo.onrender.com`), including registration/login, inventory management (`inventory_management.php`), cart checkout, and order tracking (`order-management.php`, `order-details.php`, `order-history.php`). Source code: [github.com/thunderclouds863/Peminjaman-Barang](https://github.com/thunderclouds863/Peminjaman-Barang).

## Verification

Verified multi-role login, equipment selection, checkout submission, and dashboard management flows in the live Docker deployment.

## Outcome

Delivered a working multi-role equipment loan management system that replaces paper borrowing logs with traceable digital records and live demo access.

## Reflection

Using a cart-style request flow made multi-item borrowing intuitive for first-time users while keeping approval records structured for administrators.
